[h1]Random New World 1.1.0[/h1]

More realistic coastlines, lakes, river systems and mountain ranges, plus The Wall and a new generator window. For EU5 1.4.6.

[h2]🌎 New features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]More realistic coastlines.[/b] Continents gain capes, hooked peninsulas, deep narrow-mouthed gulfs, inland seas and lagoons behind coastal spits. Some seeds join landmasses with isthmuses.
[*][b]Lakes and connected rivers.[/b] Lakes are more numerous, larger and irregular, with bays, arms and islands. Rivers flow into them and continue from an outflow at the lowest rim. Lake shores blend into the surrounding hills.
[*][b]Mountain ranges with structure.[/b] Continuous chains branch and curve, with massifs of different heights, passes, foothills and lower secondary ranges. Crests have finer ridges and slope detail, while valleys stay smoother.
[*][b]Oceans shaped by geography.[/b] Sea zones and open-ocean routes form more natural shapes. Currents follow coherent courses. Army crossings use the shortest water stretches between physical shores, including diagonal narrows. Coastal water and foam blend into the surrounding sea.
[*][b]More Pacific to explore.[/b] Ocean expansion reaches farther west. Island groups stay where there is room or move together when new continents would cover them.
[*][b]New interface and atlas.[/b] A searchable world library, resizable panels, sharper maps and ten map views, including population, climate, terrain and areas. The classic window remains available and opens automatically when needed, including under Proton.
[*][b]The Wall.[/b] A north–south continent or island chain with a mountain spine. Choose its position and width (4–44%), and allow natural straits or require continuous land. Wider Walls leave less land for the continents beside them.
[*][b]Individual resource controls.[/b] Set the frequency of each of 34 ordinary resources from 0 to 3×, alongside the precious-resource control. These change where resources occur, not production per location.
[*]Native states have stronger cultural and religious cores and more varied borders following coasts, terrain and farming corridors.
[*][b]More society settings.[/b] Target up to 60% of inhabited land in native states and set the upper peasant share from 30% to 80%. Farming and population still limit state coverage.
[*][b]Distance from the Old World.[/b] Move continents farther from the Old World's shores without reducing the amount of land; excludes The Wall and custom land images.
[*][b]Queue while generating.[/b] Prepare and queue more worlds during a run, or add a continent sketch directly. Queued worlds follow automatically; cancellation or failure leaves the rest waiting.
[*][b]Choose native countries without spoilers.[/b] Select a native country from the country list while keeping the New World map hidden.
[/list]

[h2]🔧 Fixes and improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fixed vegetation assignments that did not fit a location’s climate, especially along climate boundaries.
[*]Fixed sea-area contacts that could prevent colonial-nation eligibility in the generated Americas.
[*]Fixed a generation failure caused by exporting a strait across the map seam.
[*]Checking game files no longer freezes world selection. Manually selected game folders retain their detected build number, and the classic window’s New world action stays visible without a system icon theme.
[/list]

[quote][b]Updating:[/b] For EU5 1.4.6. Generate a new world for these changes; keep the original world mod for existing saves. World Codes from 1.0.0 can give different worlds in 1.1.0 (algorithm epoch 60). Use one RNW world at a time and restart EU5 when switching maps.[/quote]

All new controls are translated into the eleven official EU5 languages. Across the Pillars remains optional. Refined Colonization load order: Refined Colonization → generated RNW world mod.

